    "body": "Wasm compile check of head c1f127b3c (no changes made, nothing pushed).\n\nRan steps 1-4 of `web/build-app-wasm.sh` (wasi sysroot, patched flecs copies, `cargo build -p camcraft-app` and `cargo rustc -p camcraft-ui --lib --crate-type cdylib --target wasm32-unknown-unknown`, debug), skipping only the wasm-bindgen step (not installed here). Result: both compile and link with no errors, and `camcraft_ui.wasm` is produced. So the `cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")` half of `browser_files.rs` (the web_sys Blob / anchor / prompt calls) does compile.\n\nStill not exercised: wasm-bindgen glue, running in a real browser (the download, `window.prompt`, the greyed controls). Screenshots of the dialogs are still owed before review.\n",
